191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Modern organizations depend on data pipelines that feed reports, dashboards, and business KPIs. When a data-quality failure occurs, it is often noticed only after a report or metric looks wrong, and by then several downstream datasets may already be affected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Investigating such an incident requires tracing which datasets are connected, checking which quality checks failed, gathering evidence, and judging the business impact. These activities are usually carried out in separate tools and records, which makes the investigation slow and difficult to repeat.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The absence of a single system that connects incidents, lineage, quality checks, evidence, and business impact makes it difficult to find root causes quickly and to explain the importance of an incident to the business.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
